{
  "name": "MicroPython",
  "version": "v1.28.0",
  "channel": "stable",
  "releaseNotesUrl": "https://github.com/micropython/micropython/releases/tag/v1.28.0",
  "homepage": "https://micropython.org",

  "_comment": [
    "MicroPython publishes bare .bin files on micropython.org/download rather",
    "than an installer manifest, so firmforge maintains one. Every part below",
    "points at micropython.org's own resources/firmware URL — nothing is",
    "rehosted here, so no redistribution takes place and the SHA-256 values are",
    "a genuine integrity check on upstream's artifact rather than a checksum of",
    "our own copy. See plan/spec/legal-and-licensing.md.",
    "",
    "Digests and sizes were taken by downloading each file from micropython.org",
    "on 2026-08-02 and hashing it, not copied from a page that could be stale.",
    "",
    "Offsets follow micropython.org's own esptool instructions, which differ by",
    "chip: ESP32 and ESP32-S2 place the image at 0x1000, while the S3, C3 and C6",
    "place it at 0x0. Getting this wrong produces a board that does not boot,",
    "which is why they are written out per build rather than defaulted.",
    "",
    "MicroPython is MIT licensed. Flashing it replaces whatever was on the board",
    "with a Python interpreter that waits at a >>> prompt; firmforge's Terminal",
    "screen is how you talk to it afterwards."
  ],

